    "mode": "client-error-listener",
    "kind": "configured",
    "description": "The native mode plus an 'error' listener on every pooled client, added with pool.on('connect'). pg-pool removes its own client listener while a client is checked out, and Drizzle adds none, so in native mode a terminated backend's error event ends the process before db.transaction() can reject. The listener does nothing else: no rollback and no connection discard.",
    "configuration": {
      "client": "pg.Pool",
      "transaction": "db.transaction(callback)",
      "client_error_listener": "pool.on('connect', (client) => client.on('error', () => {}))"
