  "knowledge": "The framework rolls the transaction back, and PostgreSQL confirms the ROLLBACK, so the client knows that nothing committed.",
  "api_outcome": {
    "reported": "rolled_back",
    "basis": "db.transaction(callback) rejected with the error the callback threw",
    "contract": "In Drizzle ORM 0.45.4, db.transaction(callback) (NodePgSession.transaction in drizzle-orm/node-postgres/session.js) checks a client out of a pg.Pool when the client is a pool, executes BEGIN, runs the callback, executes COMMIT, and returns the callback's result. If the callback throws, it executes ROLLBACK and rethrows that error. The pg Result of COMMIT, including its command tag, is not read. A resolved call is Drizzle's report that the callback returned and COMMIT did not throw.",
    "error": {
      "class": "Error",
      "code": null,
      "message": "application error: the request fails"
    },
    "steps": {}
  },
